                <pb facs="0899" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/90: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-15T14:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:12 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>303. Department’s number 2, January 12, 7 p.m. Complications have arisen but
                    believe I can adjust entire matter satisfactorily. Pending my further
                    telegraphic report no further deportations should be made via Latvia and if any
                    now <hi rendition="#italic">en route</hi> please cable me immediately full
                    information. Attitude of the Latvian authorities most friendly and have no
                    objection to further deportations but desire in the meantime to effect necessary
                    arrangements and agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
